    {
      "title": "Resend the Gap",
      "desc": "Only the missing bytes",
      "detail": "The SACK tells the server exactly what is missing, so it resends just segment 1, and the laptop acknowledges everything. Had no ACK come back at all, timers would have stepped in: a probe after about two round trips, then a retransmission timeout (at least 200 ms on Linux).",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Resent",
          "bytes 1–1460 only"
